{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"d1f1afab5c0590bf290edc2c8f5e94835fd3bfeeac9dd49e49c25535e3d539c0","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0de8d145ff619d54aab8bb04f5aba02431f455628655d43772686c80a915e611","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a theoretical analysis of Hessian eigenvalues in deep learning. While the content is original and uses standard, non-sensitive data, it significantly violates double-blind review policies by revealing author identities and affiliations. The lack of a broader impact statement is a minor issue given the theoretical nature of the work.","paper_id":"B186cP9gx","paper_identity_sha256":"2423710f64878f6d28b77e585ad94968c2f6467fd29778684d78e64847d2a920","prompt_identity_sha256":"d128c8f37dd5c5d6add46122b9075a03560c91243cf4b7d0d291c6e48c98ee0c","raw_response_sha256":"b40fc8fc5904ef86d16f03d499fe2fdc41e94d10d548fd3e2f041b301de36c98","request_identity_sha256":"af31c997682e69bcd99bc9601fdbcbf35fc4ff69734a2f0c4a7eb11ead0a7c6f","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-005"],"review_text":"The paper focuses on the mathematical properties of the Hessian matrix in deep learning, specifically its singularity and eigenvalue distribution. The experiments utilize the MNIST dataset and synthetic Gaussian blobs, which are standard, non-sensitive benchmarks that do not involve personally identifiable information or vulnerable populations. Consequently, there are no significant ethical risks, fairness concerns, or potential harms to marginalized groups associated with this theoretical and empirical analysis. The work does not propose a new model for deployment in sensitive domains, so specific ethical mitigation strategies are not required.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-004","SRC-005"],"review_text":"The study relies on the MNIST dataset, a widely used public benchmark for handwritten digit recognition, and synthetic data generated from Gaussian distributions. The use of MNIST is standard in the field and does not raise privacy or consent issues as it does not contain sensitive personal data. The synthetic data is generated algorithmically, eliminating concerns regarding data licensing or privacy violations. The paper does not disclose any proprietary or restricted datasets, and the data usage appears compliant with standard academic research practices.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-011"],"review_text":"The submission violates double-blind review policies by explicitly listing the authors' names, institutional affiliations, and email addresses on the title page. Specifically, the text identifies Levent Sagun (New York University), Léon Bottou (Facebook AI Research), and Yann LeCun (New York University) with their contact details. Additionally, the Acknowledgments section mentions that part of the research was conducted when the first author was an intern at FAIR, further revealing the authors' identities and affiliations. These disclosures compromise the anonymity required for a fair review process.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-002","SRC-003","SRC-012"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work, including Ngiam et al. (2011), Lee et al. (2016), and Hardt et al. (2015), and acknowledges its connection to previous series of papers by Sagun et al. (2014; 2015). There is no evidence of plagiarism or uncredited reuse of material. The content appears to be original, presenting new empirical observations on the Hessian's eigenvalues. No indications of dual submission or self-plagiarism are visible in the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-008","SRC-009"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated 'Broader Impact' statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which is common for theoretical papers of this era but is increasingly expected in modern venues. However, the work is purely theoretical and empirical, focusing on optimization landscapes, and does not involve the development of new AI systems with direct societal deployment risks. The absence of a broader impact statement is a minor limitation given the current standards for responsible AI reporting, but the lack of ethical or privacy risks in the methodology mitigates this concern. No software or data licensing issues are apparent.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"8acf18f843df36df7ee11e97e7c6a87600646da27c75c8b0fa86a4cebccc8c1e","paper_id":"B186cP9gx","paper_ordinal":4,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"b40fc8fc5904ef86d16f03d499fe2fdc41e94d10d548fd3e2f041b301de36c98","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B186cP9gx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"5bcadc00a1c5043a54e4702c1ef706a670da4683591fe9203b71421543b574f2","request_identity_sha256":"af31c997682e69bcd99bc9601fdbcbf35fc4ff69734a2f0c4a7eb11ead0a7c6f","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":931,"prompt_tokens":6138,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":7069},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"af31c997682e69bcd99bc9601fdbcbf35fc4ff69734a2f0c4a7eb11ead0a7c6f","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}